{
  "version": 17,
  "calculus": {
    "name": "NJ",
    "description": "Gentzen's natural deduction for intuitionistic propositional logic (Untersuchungen über das logische Schließen, 1935), with ¬I and ¬E as rules of their own and ex falso as ⊥E; ↔ has the rules of forall x: Calgary (Magnus, Button and others, 2019). A judgement is one formula, and a hypothesis is a node of its own: a rule that discharges one takes its premise from a subproof whose hypotheses it names. Every elimination takes its major premise first.",
